), we can create a view as follows:

CREATE VIEW SalesInvoiceView AS
SELECT 
    t.TransactionID AS InvoiceNo,
    p.StockCode,
    p.Description,
    td.Quantity,
    t.InvoiceDate,
    p.UnitPrice,
    c.CustomerID,
    c.Country
FROM 
    Transactions t
JOIN 
    Transaction_Details td ON t.TransactionID = td.TransactionID
JOIN 
    Products p ON td.StockCode = p.StockCode
JOIN 
    Customers c ON t.CustomerID = c.CustomerID;
This view joins essential tables to aggregate information needed for invoice details and links them in a readable format suitable for analysis and reporting.



3. Infrastructure Requirements
Hardware:

Data Warehouse Servers: High-RAM, high-CPU, and high-storage capacity servers (e.g., Dell PowerEdge R740xd or similar). Minimum spec: 256GB RAM, 16-core CPU, 10TB HDD/SSD RAID storage.
NAS Storage: For raw data staging, use a high-capacity NAS device (e.g., NetApp FAS series).
ETL Servers: Powerful machines for ETL processing (similar specification to data warehouse servers).
Software:

Operating System: Linux (e.g., CentOS) for servers.
Database: PostgreSQL or Microsoft SQL Server for the data warehouse, considering their robustness and support for complex queries.

ETL Tools: Talend Open Studio or Pentaho Data Integration for on-premises ETL, suitable for large-scale transformations.
Version Control/Logging: Git for codebase management, and ELK Stack (Elasticsearch, Logstash, Kibana) for monitoring and logging.

